  "name": "Module 1: culture chip (demo scale)",
  "description": "DEMO SCALE: 30 x 20 mm, one fluidic layer at ONE depth (0.3 mm: every chamber, junction and channel), resin print + hot emboss. Channels are 0.2 mm wide (clamped up to the 0.2 mm open-channel floor), ports are 800 um at >= 5 mm pitch (5 of 6), and every chamber and channel names its CAD block (contracts/blocks.json). Round chambers are capped to what the lane pitch allows (seeding 3.6 mm, culture 3.6 mm, bubble trap 2 mm). There is no retention or mesh on this chip: cells stay in a lane by flow control, not by a filter. Cells load at m1_ipsc_in_1 (shared inlet, also detach reagent and harvest buffer), split three ways, each lane gets its own reagent at a T-junction, flows through an in-line bubble trap into its culture chamber and drains to the shared outlet. No valves, control ports, gas window or signals-only microgrooves: those need a second layer or sub-200 um features. GENERATED by cad/generators/m1_culture.py.",
